{"title":"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70f19eeb61e10055fb4e0c0c70ad0ee828b0ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = 84^\\circ, \\angle ABC=60^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba77cc1b81db369b1650878f92ef3decd7aa4ca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 36^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13ef86d1684ad9e3578237924ba4d47767a7ea17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}, \\overline{AC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f694ab8315c055ae7dd5d9fe5ba57a1a7c97a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> respectively. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c2c05be34487a983880615d6cc8b76bb752914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}, \\overline{AE},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65a0b904f8f63efdc2b5abfef3f4f05b2d3f990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AF}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b0acb0fa94e8be6a9b6bb5aef910041f6355aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G, H,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b9fb71fe73bafe5be4666cd597957a278860ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a948938b0f7d3d191ee6d8105121c30a32798a18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G, D, E, H, J,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> divide the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> into six minor arcs, as shown. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0561a03e0a964cae72bf718262fb4c38b3b9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{DE}+2\\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3\\cdot\\widehat{FG},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"23\" /> where the arcs are measured in degrees.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/8927c2fea7d62dafca511d88a32813611716ed6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]         import olympiad;         size(6cm);         defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));         pair B = (0, 0), A = (Cos(60), Sin(60)), C = (Cos(60)+Sin(60)/Tan(36), 0), D = midpoint(B--C), E = midpoint(A--C), F = midpoint(A--B);         guide circ = circumcircle(D, E, F);         pair G = intersectionpoint(B--D, circ), J = intersectionpoints(A--F, circ)[0], H = intersectionpoints(A--E, circ)[0];         draw(B--A--C--cycle);         draw(D--E--F--cycle);         draw(circ);  dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(D);dot(E);dot(F);dot(G);dot(H);dot(J);         label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, (0, .8));         label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, (-.8, -.8));         label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, (.8, -.8));         label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, (0, -.8));         label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, (.8, .2));         label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, (-.8, .2));         label(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, (0, .8));         label(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, (-.2, -1));         label(&quot;$J$&quot;, J, (.2, -.8)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"162\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that due to midpoints and properties of medial triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47ccd63037397743a66df3e54d8a1f38073fa16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF\\sim\\triangle FBD\\sim\\triangle AFE\\sim\\triangle EDC\\sim\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"18\" /> (and by medial triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/941b07a1afc87433c282dfe969b89ad66d1b8aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF \\cong \\triangle FBD \\cong \\triangle AFE \\cong \\triangle EDC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"319\" height=\"18\" />) . As a result, the angles and arcs are readily available. Due to inscribed angles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f213ee2a8b7976a556313cf62cd2d264c07328c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{DE}=2\\angle DFE=2\\angle ACB=2\\cdot36=72^\\circ\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"18\" />\nSimilarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246acc906b28733766a4cf0a24929591408837b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{FG}=2\\angle FDB=2\\angle ACB=2\\cdot36=72^\\circ\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>In order to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4eedbd6fbb4c18ddb3464febeffafc227300f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{HJ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" />, we use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e79e95bb2f118dac17b3144f5d6ec8830c95ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\frac{1}{2}(\\widehat{FDE}-\\widehat{HJ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"204\" height=\"38\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af319f9ccb45fb7283fdc8581c6cf0a682b26054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=84^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdde1515fef7ddcf2f524280a7abf2218bc08a83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{FDE}=360-\\widehat{FE}=360-2\\angle FDE=360-2\\angle CAB=360-2\\cdot84=192^\\circ\\]\" width=\"555\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Substituting,\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n84 &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}(192-\\widehat{HJ}) \\\\\n168 &amp;= 192-\\widehat{HJ} \\\\\n\\widehat{HJ} &amp;= 24^\\circ\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/73034fb0852e8ca3e9e0389028b74388cb01a86a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{DE}+2\\cdot\\widehat{HJ}+3\\cdot\\widehat{FG}=72+48+216=\\boxed{336}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"380\" height=\"26\" />. \n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p><p>~ Edited by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Aoum\">aoum</a>\n</p><p>Alternatively, \n</p><p>\\begin{align*} \\widehat{HJ} &amp;= \\widehat{FH} + \\widehat{JE} - \\widehat{FE} \\\\ &amp;= 2\\angle FEH + 2\\angle JFE - 2\\angle FDE \\\\ &amp;= 2 \\cdot 36^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 60^\\circ - 2 \\cdot 84^\\circ \\\\ &amp;= 24^\\circ. \\end{align*}\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/user/1096232\">Pengu14</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/5949166a20ab40a1fc34559017dea672cc79d37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle FHE \\sim \\triangle DEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/375f7644c0a99c892d96fd446615c7c59d8b8361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE \\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439ea13cfe4fa62f067f21592b71fca063ea4ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE \\parallel AB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> so all angles in each triangle will be equal by the Midline Theorem. Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7c0a9613bef9e534d04b989b31869fdaa0fb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{DE} = 2 \\cdot 36^\\circ = 72^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" /> Now, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a60f4c5d5f758ea48d9128962a91151c48bc2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FHED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, so opposite angles add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe5fe997b97dbc059b8575ca1865621f346852a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> Since we know from similar triangles that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f1e0e9ee3052e6964517d2949af6bf00b19fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FED} = 60^\\circ + 36^\\circ = 96^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6d7a7dcc303e3d5eef91d625ecd3f1eb5f4dcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{HFD} = 84^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aacd41d03177fdfb964ef0f1c0e532746dc41f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{JFE} = 60^\\circ + 36^\\circ = 96^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" /> so that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/5464ccfc8e58063cbfc125bb069e9e5cf28dfea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{JFH} = 96^\\circ - 84^\\circ = 12^\\circ \\implies \\widehat{JH} = 24^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"338\" height=\"21\" /> Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4fb7f69079618b12f3c5cc17c54f7a6c1a2a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{B} = 60^\\circ = \\frac{\\widehat{JED} - \\widehat{FG}}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"45\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5ca81a2d5dd8d3060d045bf1ad0145bb59f7bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widehat{JED} = \\widehat{DE} + \\widehat{JE} = 72^\\circ + 2(\\angle{JFE}) = 192^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"24\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c38d3d823e0b4359bc8abe68797b7de49bd316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{FG} = 192^\\circ - 120^\\circ = 72^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"202\" height=\"21\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40b8c15e10086a4f7181b448c7f95403d4fbd6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^\\circ + 2\\cdot 24^\\circ + 3\\cdot 72^\\circ = \\boxed{336^\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"244\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p><p><br />\nNOTE: Several of the letters appear to be misused. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/753d723ce394b170db089e71932abb5b129a6db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FED}=60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3ddd96ad5358d29a32d8d3c505f8411724e9f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>~Christian\n</p><p>NOTE2: It should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63cd6b790e5cd93dff451138d4a79b8091d4f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{HED}=60^\\circ + 36^\\circ = 96^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"209\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53e28607e22dce24b82196c1ad2e67298da17dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{HFD} = 180^\\circ - \\angle{HED} = 84^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"16\" />. The same for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55ea5b7d7f247dc8f196be4c2ea8dba91e4174c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{JFD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef44fb12c8700048834e5733d6337e6a8e751f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{JFE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~LANOUZHIHUN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is the median triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. It's known that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is the Nine-Point Circle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is easy to find through inscribed angles theorem, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220b84a99001bdb1147c207997cc8fae24aac079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Through Intercepted Secants Theorem, the measure of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a769d5e38f2b3b467f2913c667028a043524ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JAH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is precisely half that of the difference of the far arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and the near arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c0038c64a84032c5ca301c21f6c333aedc15b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/68927628c2f4b762ffab91fa2b83ac1d36299f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84 = 0.5 \\cdot (192-JH)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e6525b223fe07e9b52ebd08b56a4c6a14286241b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 = JH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Finally, through Alternate Interior it's obvious that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd08dc2fc54c8e63515a69753e30cfcbec5fc469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDG$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566ad2f0218f4a3bcf2723080970b1cfb04efe08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. It follows that arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951902c11a1cd39a091ea15f0f06cbc79095de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220b84a99001bdb1147c207997cc8fae24aac079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/695e277f0d0089083ebd0bbed46c543c6d237419.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DE + 2HJ + 3FG:~\\text{arcs measured in degrees}~ = 72 + 48 + 216 = \\boxed{336}^\\circ\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>The purpose of this solution is to bring up the existence of the nine-point circle. Consequently, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are not random, but are the intersections of the altitudes dropped from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. It may not be used in this problem specifically, but is great information for the long run.\n</p><p><br />\n~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JUy42ad0WOo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JUy42ad0WOo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II\" title=\"2025 AIME II\">2025 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external t